---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Engine - Julian Codespoti"
  description="The Astro + MDX + Motion declarative animation engine used to build interactive systems essays on this site."
  activeNav="framework"
>
  <main class="col-page">
    <h1 class="page-title">Declarative Scene Engine</h1>
    <p class="page-sub">
      A small Astro + MDX + Motion toolkit for building physics-driven systems diagrams without hand-rolling layout math or animation loops from scratch.
    </p>

    <div class="essay-prose">
      <p>
        Prose compiles to static HTML with zero JavaScript. Each visual is a focused React island powered by
        <code>motion/react</code> springs and SVG animations, hydrated only when scrolled into view (<code>client:visible</code>).
      </p>

      <h2>Core primitives in <code>src/engine/</code></h2>
      <ul>
        <li><code>&lt;Scene&gt;</code> frames a visual with a top bar for mode toggles or play/pause controls and a live status footer.</li>
        <li><code>useSceneActive(running)</code> combines <code>IntersectionObserver</code> and <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> so offscreen continuous animations pause automatically.</li>
        <li><code>&lt;Choice&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;ActionBtn&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;StepDots&gt;</code> provide spring-backed interactive controls and clean icon buttons.</li>
        <li><code>&lt;Term tone="copper|teal|sage|crimson"&gt;</code> ties underlined words in prose directly to the moving objects inside the next scene.</li>
        <li><code>SPRING_SNAPPY</code>, <code>SPRING_GENTLE</code>, and <code>SPRING_WEIGHTY</code> keep physical motion consistent across diagrams.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why Motion + SVG instead of one rigid chart type</h2>
      <p>
        Different systems need different visual metaphors: memory layouts glide across page boundaries with layout springs,
        network protocols stream variable-width packets across wires, back-pressure swings a mechanical intake valve,
        and dual-device state machines move cards between containers with <code>AnimatePresence</code>. Keeping the engine
        at the level of springs, visibility gates, and small interactive primitives lets any new article invent the exact
        metaphor the mechanism deserves.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
